description: Runtime crate for Wasmtime actor hosting and ephemeral tool execution
includes:
  - crates/sigil-runtime/
  - Cargo.toml
excludes:
  - crates/sigil-runtime/target/
context: |
  This crate owns the Wasmtime-backed execution environment for compiled Sigil
  modules and ephemeral ToolForge modules.
  Put capability provisioning, actor/message dispatch, runtime fuel enforcement,
  host imports, and ephemeral execution support here.

  Do not move compiler front-end logic into this crate. Compiler analysis stays in
  `sigil-compiler`; shared handoff types belong in `sigil-abi`; this crate is the
  execution environment.

  Current implemented slice:
  - `RuntimeHost` instantiates compiled Wasm with Wasmtime, bootstraps the entry
    actor, queues `Start`, and dispatches handlers through shared ABI metadata
  - runtime host imports wire `fuel_decrement`, `send`, `ask`, and `spawn`
    directly into actor/capability/message state and audit logging
  - runtime dispatch decodes the currently supported ABI payload types and tracks
    supervision, actor state transitions, and message delivery
  - the crate also exposes `execute_ephemeral`, a one-shot runtime for compiled
    tool modules with fuel metering and grant-controlled filesystem/network access
  - supporting modules isolate actor state, capabilities, grants, audit logging,
    supervision, local fuel accounting, and ephemeral host behavior
  - current bounded edges remain around actor init provisioning, spawn capability
    flow, and the set of payload/value types that can cross the runtime ABI today
related:
  - crates/.scope
  - crates/sigil-abi/.scope
  - crates/sigil-compiler/.scope
  - crates/sigil-registry/.scope
  - crates/sigil-cli/.scope
  - crates/sigil-runtime/src/.scope
tags:
  - runtime
  - rust
  - wasmtime
  - actors
  - toolforge
